By prolonging those experiences,
benefits and results arise;
the teacher taught four subdivisions of these. [N-C019](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c019) [N-C028](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c028)

The view does not remain at the Ground;
cultivation does not remain at the Ground;
realization does not remain at experience—these three,
with taking conceptual thought onto the path as the fourth,
are said to be the system of coemergent joining.
These are the temporary benefits. [N-C001](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c001) [N-C023](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c023) [N-C032](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c032)

Free from all accepting and rejecting, denying and affirming;
fearless, like a lion;
without [distinguishing] clean and filthy, like dogs and pigs;
without a fixed aim, like a mad person;
like activity untainted by stains;
without religious pretense, like a risen corpse—
if one abides in this without interruption,
it is supreme among activities. [N-C001](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c001) [N-C024](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c024) [N-C035](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c035) [N-C036](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c036)

Dharma embodiment is beyond speech, reflection, and conceptual mind;
even a genuine buddha
cannot appropriately be said to see dharma. [N-C026](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c026)

From space-like dharma embodiment, free from conceptual elaborations,
complete enjoyment embodiment arises like clouds;
from it, emanation embodiment, like rain,
acts for the benefit of sentient beings. [N-C008](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c008) [N-C030](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c030) [N-C033](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c033) [N-C037](../translations/NOTES.md#n-c037)
